{"name":"Vinho do Porto","hex":"#b31a38","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vinho","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Portuguese wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vinho"},{"term":"porto","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An apéritif made from port.","Synonym of port."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porto"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port wine","blocks":[{"text":"Port wine, or simply port, is a Portuguese fortified wine produced in the Douro Valley of northern Portugal. It is typically a sweet red wine, often served with dessert, although it also comes in dry, semi-dry, and white varieties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Port_wine.jpg/330px-Port_wine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_wine","wikidata":"Q191034"},{"title":"Vinho","blocks":[{"text":"Vinho (Korean: 빈호) is a fine dining restaurant in Seoul, South Korea. It serves contemporary cuisine, with some dishes inspired by Korean cuisine. It first opened in May 2022, and received one Michelin star for 2024."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinho","wikidata":"Q130463043"},{"title":"Porto","blocks":[{"text":"Porto, also known in English as Oporto, is the second largest city in Portugal, after Lisbon. It is the capital of the Porto District and one of the Iberian Peninsula's major urban areas. Porto city proper, which is the entire municipality of Porto, is small compared to its metropolitan area, with an estimated population of 273,476 people in a municipal area of 41.42 km2 (16 sq mi). As of 2025, the Porto metropolitan area has around 1.9 million people in an area of 2,395 km2 (925 sq mi), making it the second-largest urban area in Portugal. It is recognized as a global city with a Gamma + rating from the Globalization and World Cities Research Network."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG/330px-Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porto","wikidata":"Q36433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/500px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/1280px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG/500px-Bodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandeman cellar, Vila Nova de Gaia, Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABodega_Sandeman%2C_Vila_Nova_de_Gaia%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_06.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg/500px-VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg/500px-VinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Official guarantee label from a bottle of port","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVinhoDoPorto_Garantia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/The_Douro_Valley_vineyards.jpg/500px-The_Douro_Valley_v